# Disk & File Analysis Tools

1) ncdu

Definition:
An interactive disk usage analyzer (NCurses-based) that shows folder sizes sorted in descending order.

Use case:
Could you quickly identify which directory is consuming disk space on the servers?

> ncdu / 


2) tree

Definition:
Displays directory structure in a recursive tree format.

Use case:
Visualize project architecture or folder hierarchy.


3) bat

Definition:
Enhanced cat with syntax highlighting, line numbers, and Git integration.

Use case:
Read code files clearly inside terminal.

bat app.py

4) ranger

Definition:
Terminal-based file manager with Vim-style navigation.

Use case:
Navigate, preview, and manage files efficiently without GUI.
  
